    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d116">

                <pb facs="0159" n="85" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg85"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/5074</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Greece</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Droppers</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Athens</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-06-03T16:00:00+02:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 3, 1917, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received June 4, 1 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>345. British Minister informs me British forces are to be withdrawn from
                    Macedonia owing to difficulty of provisioning by sea. This will probably mean
                    evacuation Monastir territory. Other reasons also suspected, not disclosed,
                    possibly arrangements with Bulgarians.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Droppers</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
